package cajeta.xpu;

/**
 * Schedule — portable instruction-scheduling HINTS for a @Kernel: the controls
 * that steer how the backend interleaves matrix-core, LDS, and global-memory
 * instructions (the WMMA/memory schedule rocBLAS / Composable Kernel hand-tune).
 * Only meaningful inside @Kernel / @Device functions. See
 * docs/specs/xpu-kernel-scheduling-hints-spec.md.
 *
 * These are OPTIMIZATION DIRECTIVES: a hint never changes a kernel's result — it
 * only changes the instruction schedule, so output is identical with or without
 * it. Like AsyncCopy/CoopStage they are device-only intrinsics — the body is
 * empty and the lowering replaces each call at the @Kernel site (KernelLowering's
 * `recv == "Schedule"` dispatch → the LoweringTarget sched seams). There is no
 * real call. All operands are compile-time constants (ImmArg). Lowering per
 * backend (chosen statically):
 *   AMDGPU:  barrier → llvm.amdgcn.sched.barrier(mask); groupBarrier →
 *            llvm.amdgcn.sched.group.barrier(mask,size,syncId); priority →
 *            llvm.amdgcn.s.setprio(level); pipelineOpt → llvm.amdgcn.iglp.opt.
 *   NVPTX / SPIR-V / CPU: documented NO-OPs (the default LoweringTarget seam) —
 *            the kernel compiles and runs correctly, just without the hint.
 */
public final class Schedule {

    /**
     * Device-only intrinsic: a one-sided scheduling fence — the backend must not
     * move instructions of the classes named by `mask` across this point. `mask`
     * is a compile-time bitmask (0 = all classes; AMD sched_barrier bits, e.g.
     * 0x0020 VALU, 0x0100 DS). AMD → llvm.amdgcn.sched.barrier; no-op elsewhere.
     */
    public static void barrier(uint32 mask) {
    }

    /**
     * Device-only intrinsic: assemble an explicit instruction group of `size`
     * instructions matching `mask`, synchronized with other group-barriers
     * sharing `syncId` — lets the author hand-build a WMMA/DS/VMEM interleave.
     * All three operands are compile-time constants. AMD →
     * llvm.amdgcn.sched.group.barrier; no-op elsewhere.
     */
    public static void groupBarrier(uint32 mask, uint32 size, uint32 syncId) {
    }

    /**
     * Device-only intrinsic: set the issuing wave's scheduling priority to
     * `level` (0..3) so latency-critical waves win issue slots. `level` is a
     * compile-time constant. AMD → llvm.amdgcn.s.setprio; no-op elsewhere.
     */
    public static void priority(uint32 level) {
    }

    /**
     * Device-only intrinsic: apply the backend's canned pipeline schedule
     * `strategy` (0 = GEMM-style matrix/LDS interleave). `strategy` is a
     * compile-time constant. AMD → llvm.amdgcn.iglp.opt; no-op elsewhere.
     * Caveat: the canned strategies are MFMA/CDNA-tuned, so on RDNA WMMA this
     * may select nothing (an effective no-op) — a recorded outcome, not an error.
     */
    public static void pipelineOpt(uint32 strategy) {
    }
}
